Each line is one promise of the kernel, checked from user space.
  ok   the kernel's invariants hold at the start
  ok   the kernel has met nothing unexpected so far
  ok   system call numbers that do not exist give E_NOSYS
  ok   a message buffer outside the caller's memory gives E_FAULT
  ok   a message buffer the caller cannot write gives E_FAULT
  ok   a message buffer is checked up to its last byte
  ok   log checks the length and the address of the text
  ok   sysinfo checks where it writes and what it is asked
  ok   spawn checks the addresses of the image and of its arguments
  ok   an empty or impossible capability slot gives E_NOCAP
  ok   a capability of the wrong kind gives E_NOCAP
  ok   a copy of a capability has the same rights or fewer
  ok   a badge is set once, and only by a holder of the grant right
  ok   a dropped capability is gone
  ok   an I/O port capability reaches its ports and no others
  ok   an interrupt capability reaches its lines and no others
  ok   an interrupt line is released when its endpoint goes away
selftest: this line was written through the Log capability
  ok   the Log capability writes to the kernel log
  ok   the Info capability describes tasks and their capabilities
  ok   no task, init included, holds a capability for the reset port 0x64
  ok   the drivers refuse to crash or hang for an ordinary program
